s   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   1 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   2 Extracapsular extension  None  Other forms of axillary involvement  None  SKIN  LEFT BREAST ADDITIONAL   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are four containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left mastectomy   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm left breast mastectomy specimen which has a short suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral  The specimen is partially surfaced on the anterior aspect by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm portion of nipple and areolar skin  The nipple measures 1cm in diameter and is grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked blue anterior  black posterior  and serially sectioned  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm ill defined  indurated  gray white mass in the upper outer quadrant of the specimen which extends to 1 4cm of the posterior margin and 0 4cm of the anterior margin  Surrounding the mass is an abundant amount of dense gray white fibrous tissue  and focal cystic areas  4 2cm medial to the dominant mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm irregular  indurated gray white lesion which extends to 1 4cm of the posterior margin and 2 5cm of the anterior margin  Also identified 1 1cm medial to the second mass and 6cm from the dominant mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm ill defined  nodular indurated tan white mass which extends to 0 5cm of the posterior margin and 2 6cm of the anterior margin  The remainder of the cut surface consists mostly of dense gray white fibrous tissue with focal cystic areas consistent with fibrocystic change and lobulated tan yellow adipose tissue  The lateral aspect of the specimen is palpated and no lymph nodes are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the largest mass to the nearest posterior and anterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue between largest mass and second described mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of second lesion to the nearest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of fibrous tissue between the second lesion and third mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the third mass to nearest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue away from masses  Received fresh  labeled  additional left axillary tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm aggregate of multiple irregular tan yellow fragments of adipose tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm aggregate of lymph node bearing tan yellow portion of adipose tissue which contains multiple possible lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The lymph nodes are submitted entirely as follow  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four possible lymph nodes intact   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four possible lymph nodes intact   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One possible lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two possible lymph nodes bisected  one inked black  Received fresh  labeled  additional left breast skin   is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm irregular  unoriented portion of white skin excised to a depth of 0 6cm  The epidermal surface is grossly unremarkable  The attached soft tissue is removed and submitted entirely in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REAS